Ethical Use Clause

The Software shall not be used for any purpose that would violate basic
human rights, including but not limited to:

(a) surveillance or tracking of individuals or groups for purposes of
    persecution, oppression, or discrimination;

(b) development of weapons systems, including autonomous weapons, that
    violate international humanitarian law;

(c) activities that cause severe environmental damage or contribute to
    climate change beyond acceptable thresholds;

(d) any purpose that violates the Universal Declaration of Human Rights
    or the Geneva Conventions.

Data Protection Clause

The Software shall not be used to:

(a) collect, store, or process personal data without appropriate consent
    or legal basis;

(b) facilitate mass surveillance or monitoring of populations;

(c) enable profiling or scoring of individuals in ways that lead to
    discrimination or denial of essential services.

Humanitarian Use Priority

This Software was developed for humanitarian purposes. Contributors and
users are encouraged to prioritize uses that:

(a) support humanitarian response and disaster relief;

(b) protect vulnerable populations;

(c) promote equitable access to resources and services;

(d) advance open science and open data for public good.

